:false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","color":"b64245","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","number":16,"title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5791,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T22:40:26Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-02-10T08:15:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T23:49:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116122","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116122.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116122.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Animated Textures are currently flagged as deprecated, but have no direct workarounds for equivalent behaviors. The primary reason [for deprecation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/73492), as I can tell, was that the ProxyTexture implementation was inefficient on modern GPUs. Based on conversations in a Rendering Meeting last week, replacing the Proxy Texture backend with a DrawableTexture that draws new frames to itself should be more effective, and restore the resource's behavior.\r\n\r\nProposals based on restoring AnimatedTexture:\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13178\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11732\r\n\r\nThis PR refactors AnimatedTextures to use a DrawableTexture instead of a Proxy. The majority of the change is on the backend, the API and resource is near identical from a user perspective.\r\n\r\nAside from the straightforward stuff, internally:\r\n* AnimatedTextures need to also store their own BlitMaterial (the default uses Blend_Mix, this requires Blend_disabled)\r\n* Re-did the time logic in _update_proxy, resolving an old edge case where an AnimatedTexture would only ever progress forward one frame, regardless of time passed. It seems more straightforward/performant to me, but I may have misunderstood the nuances of the previous implementation. \r\n* Since a DrawableTexture should have a fixed size, the size of the AnimatedTexture is now established by the first frame, and every other frame is scaled to fit that quad. This is the most significant Compat change, but could be adjusted in several ways depending on feedback\r\n* I cut out the ReadWriteLock due to it introducing difficulty in rebuilding the proxy when Frame0 has its texture set.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116122/reactions","total_count":50,"+1":22,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":10,"eyes":14},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116122/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}